"smart_blocks:Computer Science/C++/call stack.md#BBFABBA6;\">When a function is called, a new **stack frame** (also known as an activation record) is \"pushed\" onto the top of the call stack. When a function finishes and returns, its stack frame is \"popped\" off the stack, and control returns to the address specified in the now-topmost frame.</mark>": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.08962724,-0.0265575,-0.01431045,-0.03935155,-0.085106,0.02437694,0.07870743,0.06686471,0.08524832,-0.00992129,0.01116513,0.00631646,-0.02527307,0.01675816,0.0167007,0.07383887,-0.03625016,0.04920732,0.00522386,-0.03274403,0.0834676,-0.04858073,-0.01916674,-0.01665492,0.04691539,0.01121811,-0.07248258,-0.03931771,-0.05215899,-0.18468875,0.034865,0.00516795,0.06595386,-0.04187755,-0.02163308,-0.06821898,-0.01971149,0.04882985,-0.05162289,0.02584218,0.02585626,0.05120975,0.00690109,-0.06731465,0.01225187,-0.04037454,-0.02619529,-0.01612164,0.035161,-0.01523208,0.01371953,-0.00456319,0.02384551,-0.04178083,0.01789048,-0.00416779,0.08936843,0.02303635,0.01146662,0.03442339,0.08522879,-0.03453133,-0.14802237,0.10614598,0.04465244,-0.00246292,0.03958674,-0.08354974,0.01768008,0.05099267,-0.05386364,0.03904409,-0.05050793,0.09882437,0.07534255,-0.09016347,-0.01849576,0.01273187,0.00787217,-0.02037658,-0.02190079,-0.0687056,-0.01722945,-0.03800482,0.02669627,0.03313471,0.00876855,-0.02491364,0.04535893,0.01347781,0.01262339,-0.00975125,0.01597311,0.09950343,-0.06436948,0.04434371,0.04949364,0.0165374,-0.09450357,0.14805605,-0.05875265,0.03503443,0.02538967,0.01031921,0.06227964,-0.04352488,-0.04462467,-0.00769016,-0.07602853,-0.00988331,-0.01176385,-0.0360627,0.09626327,-0.05171401,0.03082554,-0.03436276,0.03096874,-0.06805629,-0.0217581,-0.04402436,0.00697974,0.07704595,0.01261878,0.02326147,-0.00389515,-0.05158338,0.04239027,0.07879511,0.00860262,0.00230839,0.04533038,-0.01314826,-0.01766852,-0.0211779,-0.03424088,0.0124008,0.00853294,-0.01457162,0.01683434,-0.02